    "content": "edce2f93 Retire sctp_mtu_size_reset use sctp_pathmtu_adjustment instead\nd2d6f84a Improve sctp_get_frag_point\nc9c70231 Fix KASSERT\ndbb9f555 Improve SCTP_MAXSEG handling\n2dfe194a Improve IP level option support\na106ab8c Improve consistency\nd8563d72 Improve stream scheduler\n3e0b7c65 Cleanup stream scheduler, no functional change\n5e95fea0 Simpify stream scheduling function usage.\nb769e920 Simplify locking.\nf1175cc3 Get the outstream while holding the stcb send lock\n8dd0be72 Sync with FreeBSD.\n626bdead use appropriate argument when freeing association\n900def6c Sync with FreeBSD\n2d655480 Use explicit cast.\n078bd24a Cleanup, mostly explicit casts.\n2cd3cc0b Sync with FreeBSD\nf3df4dc3 Fix some instances of -Wunusued-but-set-variable. (#604)\n573c93b7 Improve input validation\n1ade45cb Fix errno in case of association setup failures\n965b19a8 Initialize sequence numbers for ECN correctly\nc08562ec sctp: improve input validation\ndc1aa09c Fix PR-SCTP stats\n2ceb6fb7 Improve handling of aborted associations\nf4925bd5 Improve the handling of cookie life times. The staleness reported in an error cause is in us, not ms. Enforce limits on the life time via sysct; and socket options consistently. Update the description of the sysctl variable to use the right unit. Also do some minor cleanups. This also fixes an interger overflow issue if the peer can modify the cookie. This was reported by Felix Weinrank by fuzz testing the userland stack and in https://oss-fuzz.com/testcase-detail/4800394024452096\n53579bef Whitespace changes\n25c5bb84 Cleanup.\n5cd6fe9c Remove dead stores reported by clang\n196fbbea Whitespace cleanup\nf7f9cd82 Whitespace changes\n995c0b84 Fix explicit EOR mode, thanks to Taylor Brandstetter for reporting.\n31f4eb54 Improve concurrent send() calls\n13c9337d Cleanup signing the cookie\ned764fee When using AF_CONN addresses, don't put these in the COOKIE chunk. For these addresses it is possible to reconstruct them locally. Conceptually, addresses are something to be shared with the peer, but in the case of AF_CONN this might not be the case. Therefore, zero then out. Thanks to Natalie Silvanovich of Google Project Zero for finding and reporting the issue.\neddbc5b5 Cleanups\neb611572 Don't use __Userspace_OS_* defines anymore.\n5be0c259 Don't not undefine platform specific defines anymore.\n8123b1c8 ifdef cleanup, no functional change.\na5089952 Remove support for non-head FreeBSD kernel sources.\n421fc204 Sync FBSDIDs.\na91a5988 Goodbye SCTP_SO_LOCK_TESTING.\n2ae03e53 Sync FreeBSD Ids.\n3b4263d3 Goodbye Panda.\nedd369d6 Use SCTP_SNPRINTF().\nc6c994c7 Cleanups.\nd98d2c4c Check return value of snprintf().\na0515426 Sync with FreeBSD.\nbfa530e2 Only drop DATA chunk with lower priority as specified in RFC 7496.\n0cb61bc4 Avoid underflowing a variable, which would result in taking more data from the stream queues then needed.\n23a8eca1 Undo earlier change, since it is incorrect.\nf7e08521 Fix the computation of the numbers of entries of the mapping array to look at when generating a SACK. This was wrong in case of sequence numbers wrap arounds. Thanks to Gwenael FOURRE for reporting the issue for the userland stack: https://github.com/sctplab/usrsctp/issues/462\n6ce0f8fe Zero out pointers for consistency.\nd9698aad Fix a NET_EPOCH bug.\nd07a5f27 Cleanup starting and stopping timers.\n3212d541 Get changes in again I accidently took out.\na4277725 Epochify SCTP for FreeBSD.\n61f66833 Cleanup timer handling.\n91565950 Prepare location information in preparation for integrating #417.\naa10d60b Fix build issues.\n287284c2 Sync with FreeBSD.\n81049b90 Make the message size limit used for SCTP_SENDALL configurable via a sysctl variable instead of a compiled in constant.\n790a7a25 Improve input validation for some parameters having a too small reported length.\n09768bfc Separate out SCTP related dtrace code.\nb7e98787 Ensure that local variables are reset to their initial value when dealing with error cases in a loop over all remote addresses. This issue was found and reported by OSS_Fuzz in: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=18080 https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=18086 https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=18121 https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=18163\nde8c4e36 Fix the adding of padding to COOKIE-ECHO chunks.\nd10edce4 Disable AUTH check when doing fuzz testing.\n928bf9cc Fix the check for updating an SCTP-AUTH key.\na5ce87dd Improve the handling of state cookie parameters in INIT-ACK chunks. This fixes problem with parameters indicating a zero length or partial parameters after an unknown parameter indicating to stop processing. It also fixes a problem with state cookie parameters after unknown parametes indicating to stop porcessing. Thanks to Mark Wodrich from Google for finding two of these issues by fuzz testing the userland stack and reporting them in https://github.com/sctplab/usrsctp/issues/351 and https://github.com/sctplab/usrsctp/issues/352\n0e1bc36d Sync FBSDIDs.\ne6524d54 Fix #335\n72e5cec7 Improve consistentcy.\nb59dd490 Integrate https://svnweb.freebsd.org/changeset/base/350531 and do some further cleanups.\nc82439d5 Fix the reporting of unknown parameters received in INIT chunks.\n2a5aff3b Fix two locking issue: one LOR and one issue where sbwait() was called while holding a mutex.\n64c5dd1c sctp_output: fix non-FreeBSD compilation (#324)\nf4166b34 Add MSG_EOF and MSG_EOR suppor for sendmsg() on FreeBSD.\nbfb04f3a Improve locking.\ne74b845e Fix a MacOS NKE build issue.\n1de72ec1 Sync FBSDIDs\nc518dc5a More fixes.\n* master\n  remotes/origin/2020-10-fixes\n  remotes/origin/HEAD -> origin/master\n  remotes/origin/alt-handshake-tools\n  remotes/origin/fix-545\n  remotes/origin/fuzzer\n  remotes/origin/master\n  remotes/origin/multistack\n  remotes/origin/oss-fuzz\n  remotes/origin/skunkworks\n  remotes/origin/zero\n  remotes/origin/zero-felix\n  remotes/origin/zeroRefac",
